Composed, not captured from a running server. Each line is what #595's emitters write: _sse (gateway.py:7827, 'event: {event}
data: {data}

'), _stage (gateway.py:7905, keys kind,status[,detail]), _answer_timing (gateway.py:11620-11627, keys run_id,elapsed_ms,expected_ms,deadline_ms), answer_queued/answer_admitted (gateway.py:10977-10984), all through json.dumps with its default separators. The ORDER of each stream is the one #595's tests assert (tests/perf/test_the_answer_says_how_long_it_waits.py). The times are illustrative; EXPECTED 42000 and the 900000 ceiling are the test's own constants.

